# mobile — local host runs only.
#
# Metro is NOT in Compose: it runs on the host so a phone or emulator can reach
# it and so it can use the Android SDK, which means it cannot read the repo-root
# .env. Copy this file to mobile/.env. It holds no secrets — just the API base.
# This is the second deliberate exception to "root .env only" (d-005), alongside
# frontend-next/.env.local.

# Backend base URL. Leave it unset: src/lib/api-base.ts (C1) derives the host
# from the Metro dev server, which resolves correctly on an emulator (10.0.2.2),
# a USB device and a Wi-Fi device with no per-machine config — spec §2.2.
# Set it only to override, e.g. for a device on another subnet, after
# `adb reverse tcp:3100 tcp:3100`:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3100
